.TH stralloc_catwcs 3 "Version 1.0" "December 2023" "lib/stralloc"
.SH NAME
stralloc_catwcs \- Append a wide character string to a string allocation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/stralloc.h>
.B #include <lib/utf8.h>
.B #include <wchar.h>
.sp
.BI "int stralloc_catwcs(stralloc* sa, const wchar_t* buf)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The function .BR stralloc_catwcs () appends a wide character string to a string allocation. The function takes the following parameter:
.sp
1. A pointer to a string allocation structure.
.sp
The function appends the wide character string to the string allocation.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 if the function succeeds, 0 if it runs out of memory.
.SH EXAMPLES
No examples are provided for this function.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B stralloc_cat, stralloc_catulong0, stralloc_zero
